* Two-phase interleaved buck converter built from ONE .subckt used twice.
* The two carriers are 180 degrees apart, so the inductor ripple currents
* cancel at the output at D = 0.5.
.title Interleaved buck (2 phases)
.param vin=24 fsw=50k duty=0.5

.subckt phase in out duty ph=0
S1 in sw g ron=20m eon=20u eoff=30u vref=24 iref=10
D1 0 sw vf=0.5 ron=10m
L1 sw out 50u
B1 PWM g duty freq={fsw} phase={ph}
.ends

Vin in 0 DC {vin}
B1 CONST d value={duty}
X1 in out d phase ph=0
X2 in out d phase ph=180
C1 out 0 100u
Rload out 0 2.4
.tran 0.1u 4m
.plot V(out) I(X1.L1),I(X2.L1)
.window 0.5m
.measure mean V(out)
.measure pp V(out)
.losses in=Vin out=Rload
.end
